From a4873f6679ff443005e25ea5773ed3dfd0495ddc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:04:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 230/294] gallium/pvr: fragment-only submission works at the
 kick level; TA still silent; PDS background programs filled

New experiment halves: a fragment job submitted alone (no geometry) from this context DOES get
kicked - the firmware logs "Kick 3D: ... Partial render:0" and the hardware executes until it faults
on our fragment stream. So the context/queue machinery can dispatch a job and the firmware can write
a hardware kick. The geometry kick is the specific path that produces "Kick TA" and then nothing.

Also added the fragment stream's missing background-program state, which the reference always fills
and this driver left at zero: the TPU border-colour table address and the two PDS background program
word sets (the pixel shader the 3D stage runs for tiles with no fragments, and its partial-render
variant). A zero there means "PDS heap base + 0" and the hardware executes whatever program sits at
the bottom of the PDS heap - exactly the kind of silent wrongness this project keeps paying for.

- pvr_csb_pds_bgnd_words(): packs CR_PDS_BGRND0/1/SIZEINFO.
- pvr_frag_static_stream_fill_bgnd(): patches a built stream at the layout offsets the builder uses.
- pvr_job_submit_frag_sync(): single fragment job + completion wait (PVR_PROBE_FRAG_ONLY).

The fragment-only job now still page-faults (our bgnd program is the fragment PDS program, not a real
background shader), but the kick itself is proven. Next: use that as the power-up/ordering probe for
the geometry kick, and/or make a real background program.

Verification: probe ALL PASS under the shim; traces archived in open-driver-perf/captures/real-runs/.
